        "body": "The draft dust settles in Washington, and the Commanders - fresh off a <strong>5-12 slog that left them third in the NFC East, six games back</strong> - emerged with a rookie haul screaming redemption. General manager Adam Peters pounced on Georgia quarterback Carson Beck in the first round, a cannon-armed maestro whose 41 completions for 455 yards in his final college blur fit Kliff Kingsbury's air raid like a glove - imagine him slinging to Terry McLaurin amid a revamped line. Round two brought edge rusher Nic Scourton from Texas A&M, a 6-foot-4 wrecking ball with 11 sacks last fall, primed to terrorize from Day 1 and plug the pass-rush void that doomed last year's collapse. Depth-chart ripples hit hard: Scourton slides in opposite Jonathan Allen, while undrafted gems like Virginia Tech corner J.R. Hood and Miami safety Mishael Powell clog the secondary, forcing veterans to earn snaps. Beck's arm could ignite 4,000-yard dreams if he grips the starter's reins early - don't sleep on this kid carrying a franchise gunning for playoffs. <strong>OTAs next month will reveal if this class gels or merely papers over the 5-12 scars - watch Beck's first snaps against the ones.</strong>",
